00:09:32.304 --> 00:09:34.624
Delwath: and like, "We thought of you kind of."

00:09:35.884 --> 00:09:37.224
Delwath: Um, [laughs] we thought of you.

00:09:37.224 --> 00:09:38.224
Delwath: It just made us just...

00:09:39.124 --> 00:09:43.464
Delwath: Just like, "We thought you might be interested in news of your enemy."

00:09:46.124 --> 00:09:48.824
DM: And what are you... Like what are you trying to convince her to?

00:09:48.944 --> 00:09:55.924
Delwath: I'm asking... I'm basically telling her we're planning on fighting this dragon, and does she know anything that would help us?

00:09:56.444 --> 00:09:56.544
Unknown: Hmm.

00:09:59.284 --> 00:09:59.584
Unknown: Well, first-

00:09:59.624 --> 00:10:00.164
Unknown: Well, which, which main-

00:10:00.204 --> 00:10:04.504
Kenzo: Maybe, maybe, maybe first we just, we just say like, "Uh," and just, just, just see her reaction-

00:10:04.604 --> 00:10:04.644
Delwath: Right

00:10:04.644 --> 00:10:07.044
Kenzo: ... to the news about Cha'mutte's daughter, and does she like, does she like-

00:10:07.084 --> 00:10:07.804
Delwath: That's true actually

00:10:07.804 --> 00:10:10.064
Kenzo: ... does she like recoil or is she neutral?

00:10:10.084 --> 00:10:10.844
Kenzo: Is she like, you know?

00:10:11.944 --> 00:10:14.344
Delwath: Yeah. Watch her, watch her carefully, like insight, like-

00:10:14.404 --> 00:10:14.824
Unknown: Yeah. Oh, yeah, yeah

00:10:14.824 --> 00:10:15.284
Delwath: ... does-

00:10:15.324 --> 00:10:17.404
DM: Yeah, go ahead and make an insight check.

00:10:17.404 --> 00:10:18.124
Delwath: Does she like

00:10:19.384 --> 00:10:22.064
Delwath: react like [die rolling]

00:10:22.064 --> 00:10:22.984
Unknown: D20. Eight.

00:10:22.984 --> 00:10:23.024
Unknown: 20.

00:10:23.024 --> 00:10:28.404
Delwath: Does she like react like there is no, like, "Cha'mutte's daughter, I've never heard of this," or like doesn't seem to care or?

00:10:28.404 --> 00:10:30.764
DM: She's... I mean, she doesn't seem particularly

00:10:34.004 --> 00:10:36.024
DM: not... I mean, she's not like, "Oh, yes."

00:10:36.024 --> 00:10:37.224
DM: Or, you know?

00:10:37.224 --> 00:10:45.104
DM: She doesn't seem like... She, she's sort of listening carefully and kind of her attitude is kind of like, "And what do you want?

00:10:45.104 --> 00:10:47.144
DM: Why are you bothering me? What do you want from me?

00:10:47.144 --> 00:10:49.624
DM: Unless you're gonna... Unless you're planning on freeing me,

00:10:51.704 --> 00:10:53.184
DM: what kind of help do you expect?"

00:10:55.584 --> 00:10:55.784
Delwath: Uh,

00:10:57.004 --> 00:10:59.504
Delwath: I'll... I mean, the first thing is I, I thought she would

00:11:01.704 --> 00:11:04.324
Delwath: appreciate the information.

00:11:05.344 --> 00:11:10.044
Delwath: But of course, if it's of no value to her, that's fine.

00:11:10.044 --> 00:11:13.484
Delwath: And does she know anything about Cha'mutte's daughter?

00:11:14.164 --> 00:11:16.264
Delwath: Did this creature exist in her time?

00:11:17.124 --> 00:11:18.424
Delwath: Had she heard rumors?

00:11:18.424 --> 00:11:19.064
Unknown: Maybe.

00:11:20.964 --> 00:11:23.884
DM: My concern was always my

00:11:24.724 --> 00:11:25.384
DM: domain.

00:11:29.424 --> 00:11:31.684
DM: Cha'mutte barged in unwelcome,

00:11:32.744 --> 00:11:35.364
DM: and I would be very happy to just go back to my life.

00:11:36.764 --> 00:11:39.224
DM: I want nothing to do with dragons or

00:11:40.804 --> 00:11:41.924
DM: great quests.

00:11:43.524 --> 00:11:45.644
DM: She comes across as pretty parochial.

00:11:47.404 --> 00:11:47.524
Delwath: Hmm.

00:11:50.044 --> 00:11:52.284
Kenzo: [clears throat] So-

00:11:52.284 --> 00:11:54.504
DM: I might be willing to help if you will

00:11:56.764 --> 00:11:58.024
DM: restore me to my

00:12:00.264 --> 00:12:01.184
DM: proper place.

00:12:01.184 --> 00:12:05.324
Kenzo: [clears throat] Do you know how long you've been in there?

00:12:07.544 --> 00:12:09.744
DM: Well, it sounds like hundreds of years.

00:12:11.424 --> 00:12:13.084
Wellby: Other people live in your territory now

00:12:15.832 --> 00:12:18.572
DM: It was always an out of the way place in the world.

00:12:18.572 --> 00:12:28.672
Unknown: [clears throat] So

00:12:28.672 --> 00:12:28.872
Unknown: look,

00:12:30.672 --> 00:12:30.872
Unknown: uh,

00:12:32.032 --> 00:12:32.452
Kenzo: personally,

00:12:33.272 --> 00:12:35.052
Kenzo: and again, this is just me speaking here,

00:12:36.272 --> 00:12:36.512
Unknown: um,

00:12:37.492 --> 00:12:38.932
Kenzo: I don't much like the idea of like...

00:12:39.952 --> 00:12:44.592
Kenzo: I, I don't know anything about your, your past, what's, what's been happening for you, but,

00:12:45.612 --> 00:12:45.872
Unknown: um,

00:12:47.252 --> 00:12:47.892
Kenzo: I think there's

00:12:49.712 --> 00:12:55.012
Kenzo: a possibility that we could imagine a scenario where you could come out of that mirror.

00:12:55.012 --> 00:12:55.352
Unknown: I think

00:12:56.772 --> 00:13:02.592
Kenzo: the world is shifting. There's a lot of things happening right now, and, um, us figuring out how to

00:13:04.352 --> 00:13:09.892
Kenzo: [clears throat] deal with, uh, Cha'mutte's daughter is of critical importance in this moment in history.

00:13:10.952 --> 00:13:11.312
Unknown: And

00:13:12.652 --> 00:13:14.252
Kenzo: yeah, I mean, this is just me speaking.

00:13:14.252 --> 00:13:24.272
Kenzo: I think we can all talk a little bit about this more, but I could imagine a way in which if you were able to provide information that could be critical, of, of critical use for us in

00:13:24.272 --> 00:13:27.992
Kenzo: this upcoming engagement, that we could potentially figure something out.

00:13:31.312 --> 00:13:36.252
Delwath: Freedom, I'll say this in Dunmari, freedom would require

00:13:37.452 --> 00:13:39.152
Unknown: fighting us, with us, no?

00:13:39.852 --> 00:13:41.852
Delwath: We're not gonna let her go just for telling us things.

00:13:44.012 --> 00:13:46.312
Wellby: We're not gonna put her on the battlefield with us either.

00:13:46.872 --> 00:13:47.752
Unknown: No, I'm not saying right now.

00:13:47.752 --> 00:13:49.372
Seeker: Then I don't see any way to let her go.

00:13:50.032 --> 00:13:50.332
Unknown: Not now.

00:13:50.412 --> 00:13:51.632
Delwath: Information's not worth it.

00:13:51.832 --> 00:13:56.252
Wellby: I mean, if she's got teleport, as soon as she's out of that mirror, she's out of our control.

00:13:59.092 --> 00:14:00.412
Delwath: That's why I don't think we should free her.

00:14:00.912 --> 00:14:03.432
Kenzo: Yeah. Do you have any information that is helpful to us?

00:14:06.132 --> 00:14:06.552
Wellby: Well, actually,

00:14:07.592 --> 00:14:09.312
Wellby: do you wanna see Cha'mutte's daughter dead?

00:14:09.312 --> 00:14:11.312
Wellby: 'Cause that's our plan for the day.

00:14:11.312 --> 00:14:14.112
Wellby: And if you don't, and if it doesn't matter, we can call it a day.

00:14:14.352 --> 00:14:14.492
Unknown: Yeah.

00:14:14.952 --> 00:14:15.492
Wellby: But if you do,

00:14:16.512 --> 00:14:16.972
Wellby: let's talk.

00:14:17.692 --> 00:14:20.112
Kenzo: And if you have anything that can help us, let's talk.

00:14:21.732 --> 00:14:23.652
Delwath: I mean, didn't she sort of already say no, she did, but...

00:14:24.232 --> 00:14:24.572
Unknown: If either of the-

00:14:24.572 --> 00:14:26.412
Wellby: Just wanna be real direct. If our interests don't align-

00:14:26.572 --> 00:14:26.992
Unknown: Yeah, then that's-

00:14:26.992 --> 00:14:27.512
Wellby: ... we'll move on.

00:14:27.552 --> 00:14:28.292
Kenzo: That, that's fine.

00:14:35.112 --> 00:14:40.492
DM: How, how, so what did, wait, what did, uh, did you tell her the whole story about Dimitaur, where you were or where Cha'mutte was?

00:14:40.552 --> 00:14:43.792
Kenzo: No. Just, just that we're, we're, we're gonna go, go, go kill Cha'mutte's daughter.

00:14:48.592 --> 00:14:53.792
DM: I don't see why I would have a quarrel with Cha'mutte's daughter unless she was threatening my territory.

00:14:55.732 --> 00:14:56.132
DM: Is she?

00:14:56.132 --> 00:14:57.472
Unknown: [sighs]

00:14:57.472 --> 00:15:00.332
DM: I would say no, as I currently have no territory.

00:15:02.432 --> 00:15:03.292
Unknown: Hmm. All right.

00:15:04.412 --> 00:15:04.532
Unknown: Well...

00:15:04.552 --> 00:15:06.332
DM: Unless you're offering me territory.

00:15:07.712 --> 00:15:09.932
Kenzo: But do you, do you have any information to help us?

00:15:10.052 --> 00:15:10.172
Wellby: What-

00:15:10.312 --> 00:15:10.652
Unknown: Either way?

00:15:11.932 --> 00:15:14.572
Wellby: What if she was keeping some part of Cha'mutte alive?

00:15:14.572 --> 00:15:15.332
Wellby: What if she was

00:15:16.352 --> 00:15:19.472
Wellby: protecting something or planning?

00:15:19.472 --> 00:15:21.092
Wellby: As it's been described, she's

00:15:23.072 --> 00:15:26.732
Wellby: serving some purpose that she can't move from.

00:15:26.732 --> 00:15:28.032
DM: That's fine by me.

00:15:28.032 --> 00:15:31.372
DM: I'm not sure what quarrel you think I have with Cha'mutte other than

00:15:33.332 --> 00:15:37.072
DM: all I want is my own kingdom to run as I see fit.

00:15:37.292 --> 00:15:39.712
Wellby: You're the least vengeful hobgoblin I've ever met.

00:15:40.172 --> 00:15:41.852
Kenzo: Listen, this is really simple.

00:15:41.852 --> 00:15:44.692
Kenzo: Do you have any information at all that could be useful to us in this?

00:15:45.212 --> 00:15:45.452
Unknown: And if not-

00:15:45.472 --> 00:15:46.612
DM: I have lots of information

00:15:46.612 --> 00:15:48.832
Kenzo: ... about Cha'mutte's daughter that'd be useful in a, in a battle?

00:15:49.392 --> 00:15:49.732
DM: Mm.

00:15:52.372 --> 00:15:53.372
Kenzo: Doesn't really seem like it.

00:15:55.172 --> 00:15:56.212
Kenzo: I think we're probably done here.

00:15:57.112 --> 00:15:58.972
Seeker: Did you, uh, did you know your grandfather?

00:15:58.972 --> 00:16:05.052
DM: [scoffs] You know that, I'm not sure what that has to do with anything.

00:16:06.792 --> 00:16:08.592
Seeker: Well, he was a

00:16:09.792 --> 00:16:11.512
Seeker: powerful wizard as far as we know.

00:16:12.472 --> 00:16:13.732
Unknown: How do we know that, by the way?

00:16:13.732 --> 00:16:14.372
Seeker: Well, he created-

00:16:14.412 --> 00:16:15.272
DM: He made the mirror.

00:16:15.272 --> 00:16:19.672
Seeker: He created this mirror that you're, you yourself are trapped inside of, even now.

00:16:20.552 --> 00:16:22.232
Seeker: It's been a very powerful tool for us.

00:16:27.392 --> 00:16:28.072
Seeker: You too

00:16:29.892 --> 00:16:31.292
Seeker: could have a legacy like that,

00:16:32.892 --> 00:16:35.452
Seeker: but it takes intervening in the world.

00:16:35.452 --> 00:16:37.252
DM: Keeping people imprisoned forever?

00:16:39.012 --> 00:16:40.712
DM: I don't know if that is my desire.

00:16:40.712 --> 00:16:43.592
DM: Well, yes, there are some people I keep imprisoned forever.

00:16:46.252 --> 00:16:47.292
DM: That's certainly true.

00:16:49.952 --> 00:16:52.512
Seeker: Our group has used this mirror created by your grandfather

00:16:53.672 --> 00:16:54.232
Unknown: to,

00:16:56.392 --> 00:17:02.352
Seeker: in the ways that we have access to, nudge the history of the whole world towards peace.

00:17:03.192 --> 00:17:04.052
DM: Towards peace?

00:17:04.572 --> 00:17:05.292
Unknown: We have.

00:17:05.292 --> 00:17:06.872
DM: That seems like a rather

00:17:09.012 --> 00:17:10.952
DM: small-minded use of such a tool.

00:17:11.612 --> 00:17:12.412
Seeker: How would you use it?

00:17:16.072 --> 00:17:17.932
DM: She's look, she looks kind of thoughtful.

00:17:18.152 --> 00:17:19.772
Delwath: Here's where the lack of soul comes out.

00:17:19.772 --> 00:17:21.312
Unknown: [laughing] Tell it.

00:17:23.672 --> 00:17:26.032
DM: Well, it seems an easy way to gain territory.

00:17:27.432 --> 00:17:28.512
DM: Just trap the ruler

00:17:29.932 --> 00:17:30.672
DM: and move in.

00:17:32.212 --> 00:17:33.812
Seeker: And that's how you'd use the mirror if you had it?

00:17:36.592 --> 00:17:40.732
DM: I'm sure if I had time to think, I'd come up with other creative uses, yes.

00:17:41.452 --> 00:17:44.592
Seeker: We've had a great deal of such time and made many creative uses.

00:17:47.892 --> 00:17:48.712
DM: Interesting.

00:17:50.572 --> 00:17:53.072
DM: And you too desire territory?

00:17:53.072 --> 00:17:58.332
DM: Perhaps I could work with you. [gasps] Look in curiously at Seeker.

00:17:58.332 --> 00:18:03.412
Seeker: [laughs] [clears throat] Surely there's a way our interests could align.

00:18:04.292 --> 00:18:08.872
Kenzo: Can we, is this like, does she ha- I mean, it doesn't seem like you have any information to help us.

00:18:09.972 --> 00:18:14.612
DM: I mean, Kenzo sense with your insight is, I mean, she's trying to string you along.

00:18:14.652 --> 00:18:16.572
Kenzo: Yeah, exactly. Uh, this is... I think we're done here.

00:18:16.992 --> 00:18:21.840
Kenzo: I don't think there's- Just telepathically.

00:18:21.860 --> 00:18:26.060
Kenzo: Like, if our goal is to try to get information to help us with this battle, this is not the way.

00:18:26.060 --> 00:18:26.460
Unknown: There's, this is a dead end.

00:18:26.480 --> 00:18:27.740
Wellby: No, we don't have shared interests here.

00:18:28.080 --> 00:18:28.780
Kenzo: This is a dead end.

00:18:29.640 --> 00:18:29.820
Wellby: Mm-hmm.

00:18:29.860 --> 00:18:30.540
Unknown: Yep, I agree.

00:18:33.300 --> 00:18:33.500
Unknown: Well,

00:18:34.640 --> 00:18:35.480
Kenzo: we'll see you soon.

00:18:35.480 --> 00:18:37.040
DM: [laughs] She's like, "Wait."

00:18:37.040 --> 00:18:39.480
Unknown: [laughs]

00:18:39.480 --> 00:18:41.580
DM: I was thinking about the... I was thinking about...

00:18:41.580 --> 00:18:46.700
Unknown: [laughs]

00:18:46.700 --> 00:18:47.940
Delwath: [coughs] All right, well that didn't pan out.

00:18:48.620 --> 00:18:50.060
Kenzo: It's okay. They don't all do.

00:18:50.360 --> 00:18:51.300
Delwath: Although it occurs to me,

00:18:53.260 --> 00:18:57.000
Delwath: if we knew of a place where there was an expansionist hobgoblin leader

00:18:59.340 --> 00:19:03.480
Delwath: who was trying to conquer a human kingdom or push and expand their territory,

00:19:04.980 --> 00:19:05.800
Delwath: dropping her in

00:19:07.140 --> 00:19:08.720
Unknown: might actually be useful.

00:19:08.720 --> 00:19:09.040
Unknown: Why?

00:19:10.280 --> 00:19:16.320
Delwath: Because she would try and conquer the hobgoblin territory from the other hobgoblin leader and cause a civil war.

00:19:18.240 --> 00:19:24.740
Delwath: And she seems like the kind of person who, if she won, might be a lot more content, right?

00:19:24.740 --> 00:19:33.240
Delwath: Like she strikes me a little bit as the kind of leader who, given a well-defended border and absolute control over her kingdom-

00:19:33.620 --> 00:19:34.280
Kenzo: Would just stay there

00:19:34.280 --> 00:19:35.220
Delwath: ... would just stay there.

00:19:35.220 --> 00:19:41.080
Wellby: Maybe, but maybe the lesson from the last time she had a well-defended border and absolute control was that that wasn't enough.

00:19:41.080 --> 00:19:41.660
Delwath: That's true also.

00:19:41.660 --> 00:19:43.080
Wellby: And that you have to continually-

00:19:43.120 --> 00:19:45.520
Kenzo: Well, and also why, why wouldn't she join forces with the, uh...

00:19:45.540 --> 00:19:46.260
Kenzo: I mean

00:19:46.260 --> 00:19:47.340
Delwath: 'Cause she wants to lead.

00:19:47.440 --> 00:19:48.140
Kenzo: But in the short term-

00:19:49.100 --> 00:19:49.720
Delwath: Mm

00:19:49.720 --> 00:19:50.860
Delwath: ... that's a risk.

00:19:50.860 --> 00:19:52.280
Wellby: I think we're not letting her out, are we?

00:19:52.420 --> 00:19:56.440
Unknown: I don't think so. [laughs]

00:19:56.440 --> 00:19:56.600
Delwath: [laughs]

00:19:56.680 --> 00:19:59.600
Delwath: Thomas just looks at you like, "Yeah, yeah, okay.

00:20:00.080 --> 00:20:01.920
Delwath: C- Maybe you should say the elf was right."

00:20:02.260 --> 00:20:03.860
Kenzo: I, uh, so, so...

00:20:03.860 --> 00:20:05.480
Delwath: [laughs]

00:20:05.480 --> 00:20:06.540
Wellby: Well, you can still be wrong.

00:20:06.540 --> 00:20:07.300
Kenzo: Both things... Exactly.

00:20:07.320 --> 00:20:07.500
Wellby: Yeah, yeah.

00:20:07.500 --> 00:20:07.520
Unknown: Yeah.

00:20:07.520 --> 00:20:07.640
Wellby: And, and-

00:20:07.640 --> 00:20:09.020
Kenzo: Both things can be true, yeah.

00:20:09.020 --> 00:20:12.160
Kenzo: We're not letting her out, and the elf was wrong simultaneously.

00:20:12.160 --> 00:20:12.780
Delwath: [laughs]

00:20:12.780 --> 00:20:14.140
Kenzo: Yeah. The universe was not destroyed, see?

00:20:14.340 --> 00:20:15.260
Unknown: So... [laughs]

00:20:15.260 --> 00:20:17.400
Delwath: [laughs]

00:20:17.420 --> 00:20:17.820
Wellby: All right.

00:20:19.680 --> 00:20:21.240
Seeker: So, all right.

00:20:21.240 --> 00:20:21.480
Unknown: Well-

00:20:21.520 --> 00:20:22.440
Delwath: So

00:20:22.440 --> 00:20:23.800
Kenzo: ... is there anything we can learn about

00:20:25.160 --> 00:20:25.740
Kenzo: the dragon

00:20:27.080 --> 00:20:29.020
Kenzo: other than just, you know, barging into the lair?

00:20:29.039 --> 00:20:29.819
Kenzo: Can we sneak into the lair?

00:20:30.300 --> 00:20:30.460
Delwath: Well-

00:20:30.460 --> 00:20:33.560
Kenzo: Can you use your animal, uh, animal, animal, um-

00:20:33.720 --> 00:20:34.400
Delwath: Animal shapes thing?

00:20:34.620 --> 00:20:35.940
Kenzo: Yeah. Let's see if we could.

00:20:36.000 --> 00:20:36.720
Delwath: Before...

00:20:37.680 --> 00:20:39.400
Delwath: We should consider whether we want

00:20:40.520 --> 00:20:41.240
Delwath: to work with her.

00:20:41.700 --> 00:20:42.000
Unknown: Parley?

00:20:42.560 --> 00:20:43.440
Delwath: Yeah.

00:20:43.500 --> 00:20:45.740
Seeker: We can also validate the question of

00:20:46.560 --> 00:20:48.720
Seeker: interdimensional portal or not using that wand.

00:20:49.160 --> 00:20:51.320
Kenzo: We already know that she's not, she's not in there.

00:20:51.320 --> 00:20:52.980
Kenzo: It's inter... We already know it's interdi- I, I can sense her

00:20:52.980 --> 00:20:54.340
Delwath: Kenzo couldn't sense her.

00:20:54.440 --> 00:20:54.840
Unknown: Oh, okay.

00:20:54.860 --> 00:20:57.400
Delwath: Yeah. She's either warded in some fashion or interdimensional.

00:20:57.420 --> 00:20:58.400
Unknown: She... But is there any-

00:20:58.400 --> 00:20:58.840
Delwath: And probably couldn't-

00:20:58.900 --> 00:21:00.200
Kenzo: Is there anything that can ward...

00:21:00.720 --> 00:21:06.980
DM: Yeah, so there's like... I mean, there's a 8th level spell called Mind Blank that makes you completely undetectable to any magic-

00:21:07.140 --> 00:21:07.260
Unknown: Mm

00:21:07.260 --> 00:21:10.520
DM: ... or other sense that would detect creatures of your type.

00:21:10.520 --> 00:21:11.860
Seeker: So we may as well use the wand and just-

00:21:11.920 --> 00:21:12.040
Unknown: Yeah

00:21:12.040 --> 00:21:13.420
Seeker: ... make sure we know exactly where it is.

00:21:14.080 --> 00:21:15.200
Delwath: What does the wand do again?

00:21:15.200 --> 00:21:15.920
Seeker: Detects the nearest-

00:21:15.940 --> 00:21:17.280
DM: It detects the nearest portal.

00:21:17.440 --> 00:21:18.000
Wellby: What's the range?

00:21:19.540 --> 00:21:20.400
Seeker: I think it's any range.

00:21:20.460 --> 00:21:21.060
Wellby: Oh, okay.

